            ReleaseNotes = '1.4.0: Bundles two more collectors, RemoteSystem (the computer, its hardware, hotfixes and features) and RemoteEventLog (the event logs), so Get-RemoteBaseline runs seven collectors and -Type accepts System and EventLog, with seven selected by default. The run order is System, RSOP, ScheduledTask, SecEdit, Service, Firewall, EventLog, so RemoteSystem reads the SID reference and the six others are called with -SkipSidReference. results.csv and run.json carry the per-type Status and ErrorCount columns of the two new collectors, in that order. Csv guard: a text cell of results.csv that starts with =, +, - or @ is written with one apostrophe in front, so a spreadsheet shows it as text and does not run it as a formula, and run.json holds the exact value. The test suite runs from any folder, also one with square brackets in its name. Every bundled collector writes application package SIDs and capability SIDs to appcontainers.json and appcontainers.csv, and accounts.json and accounts.csv hold accounts only. New -SkipDismFeatures switch: it is handed to RemoteSystem, which then does not read the Windows feature list from DISM, the one read that makes Windows append to its own dism.log on the target, and run.json gains SkipDismFeatures after UseSSL. Output convention 1.5 (run.json SchemaVersion 1.5). Bundled collectors: RemoteEventLog 1.0.0, RemoteFirewall 1.5.0, RemoteRSOP 1.5.0, RemoteScheduledTask 1.6.0, RemoteSecEdit 1.8.0, RemoteService 1.7.0, RemoteSystem 1.0.0. 1.3.0: Bundles RemoteService 1.6.0. In the services files of each host every service also lists the services and groups it depends on, the services that depend on it and its ServiceDll, services.csv gains the columns ServiceDll and ServiceDllPath, every ServiceDll file is a row in binaries.json and binaries.csv and counts in the binary counts, and summary.json and system.json gain ServiceDllCount and RegistryDurationMs. Output convention 1.4 is unchanged. Bundled collectors: RemoteFirewall 1.4.0, RemoteRSOP 1.4.0, RemoteScheduledTask 1.5.0, RemoteSecEdit 1.7.0, RemoteService 1.6.0. 1.2.0: -OutputFormat (Json, Csv or Both, default Json) is passed to every bundled collector that has the parameter. results.csv of this module is written only for Csv and Both, while run.json always holds the results and records OutputFormat. -OutputPath is optional and defaults to the current location. A bundled collector without -OutputFormat is called without it and its files stay as they are. Output convention 1.4 (run.json SchemaVersion 1.4). Bundled collectors: RemoteFirewall 1.4.0, RemoteRSOP 1.4.0, RemoteScheduledTask 1.5.0, RemoteSecEdit 1.7.0, RemoteService 1.5.0. 1.1.0: the SID reference (MachineSid, DomainSid, ComputerAccountSid, DomainNetbiosName) is read once per host and run by the first selected collector, every later collector is called with -SkipSidReference, and host.json carries the four values after MachineGuid. The values appear with RemoteRSOP 1.3.0, RemoteScheduledTask 1.4.1, RemoteSecEdit 1.6.0, RemoteService 1.4.0 and RemoteFirewall 1.3.0, and a bundled collector without the switch is called without it. Output convention 1.3 (run.json SchemaVersion 1.3). 1.0.0: first release. One function, Get-RemoteBaseline, runs any combination of five bundled collectors (Firewall, RSOP, ScheduledTask, SecEdit, Service) against local and remote computers and arranges their output per host, with run.json, results.csv, a SHA-256 manifest and an optional zip. Bundled collectors, unchanged: RemoteFirewall 1.2.0, RemoteRSOP 1.2.0, RemoteScheduledTask 1.3.0, RemoteSecEdit 1.5.0, RemoteService 1.3.0. Output convention 1.2.'
